# ARCC historical market-implied risk loop

Locked after source acquisition/preflight, before analytical outputs. Execution
2026-11-04 by the current host model with preceding context; no agents, provider
calls, credentials or native accepted heads. Historical 2024-12-31 evaluated
values, not current research or a point-in-time availability backtest.

CP-0 admits the retained ARCC FY2024 annual report and prior executed July 2029
note supplement, plus the downloaded official Treasury FY2024 CSV and retained
public-body capture. Do not change prior run directories. A focused CP-1 extracts
the actual principal/carrying/fair values and note terms. CP-3D performs the
market map and CP-3 then actually consumes it; source admission is not analysis.

Select the broader CP-3D market/convention/curve/technical questions and retain
later source/number safeguards. Pin exact methodology and unchanged helper files.
Current six-heading Markdown transport governs; historical native-head, export,
staff/controller and full-run labels are not inherited gates. Do not narrow the
analysis to the later runtime's floating-loan simple-discount formula.

Cover all ten functional views: instrument/evidence, quoted/evaluated levels,
issuer curve, benchmark/peer alignment, model-implied loss, liquidity/technicals,
fundamental reconciliation, price sensitivity, monitoring and gaps. Separate
observations, calculations, assumptions and interpretation throughout. No buy/
sell/hold recommendation, security ranking or position size belongs to CP-3D.

The filing's aggregate Level-2 debt fair values are issuer estimates from market
rates/quotes if available, in rounded USD millions; they are not dated executable
bid/offer quotes. Fair value/principal*100 is a calculated evaluated equivalent,
not a directly observed clean price. Clean versus dirty treatment, accrued basis
and exact quote time are not established. Retain both conditional interpretations
for the July 2029 note, plus rounding sensitivity; never silently settle that gap.
Use contractual fixed coupon 5.950%, not issuer post-swap effective 6.040%; issuer
hedges do not change the noteholder coupon. Keep principal, carrying/hedge
accounting and fair value distinct. Source dashes stay absent.

Positive pricing work: actual July 2029 terms and fair-value equivalent, dated
remaining coupon/redemption legs under an explicitly analyst-selected 30E/360
scenario convention, semiannual nominal discounting, and a separately labeled
clean/dirty input sensitivity at 2024-12-31. This convention is not asserted to
be the exact dealer or legal end-of-month convention. The existing high-level
bond helper refuses dated/accrued/stub inputs; preserve that refusal. Reuse its
unchanged low-level PV/yield primitives on explicit supplied cash flows, with
independent high-precision Decimal PV/root checks. This proves the case
calculation, not a general production dated-bond adapter. Never report its default
ACT/365F/coupon-date convention as if it governed these supplied flows.

Compare maturity redemption with the source's June 15, 2029 par-call leg,
including the partial final coupon. The earlier Treasury+30bp make-whole formula
is contingent; two calculated terminal legs are not complete yield-to-worst/OAS.
Do not manufacture a fixed early-call schedule. Other notes provide actual
evaluated-curve context but no unreviewed contractual yield or ranking.

Use the actual same-date USD Treasury par curve; keep exact maturity header/date
mapping and label any maturity interpolation as analyst calculation. A simple
yield-minus-interpolated-par spread is not OAS, Z-spread or loan discount margin.
Benchmark quotes and issuer evaluated values have different depth/timing. No
external corporate peer/index/rating signal is supplied by Treasury rates.

Show conditional model loss break-even at explicitly assumed 20/40/60% recovery
and a stated horizon, with formula, discounting/credit-liquidity/option limitations.
It is not a factual or market-quoted default probability. Reprice the stated
cash flows for +/-100bp yield and report the actual conditional price moves;
do not claim credit-only shocks. Unknown execution depth, flows and correlations
remain unknown. Issue size does not prove liquidity.

Check actual output against instructions, literal primary sources and independent
arithmetic; repair only an observed issue and preserve completed first answers.
CP-3 opens the checked output and uses the actual pricing/convention findings and
limitations. CP-3's other analytical/portfolio phases remain separate work rather
than passing on a gap-only refusal. Keep one case verification record. Populated
delivery, Model and CP-OS still govern end-to-end completion.
